  "description": "QILBAR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H102 Ho4 Mn2 N4 O34,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 9 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.374-3.914 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.24-122.02°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [MnIII2HoIII4(L1)2(L2)2(μ3-OH)4(μ1,3-pivalate)6(NO3)2]·2CH3CN (C74H108N6O34Mn2Ho4; CCDC C70H102Ho4Mn2N4O34·2(C2H3N)). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Ho(III).",
